Aerie-Purpose: Refuse every URL request the browser makes on its own unless it is on the reviewed allowlist (docs/network-endpoints.md), so a request that a later Chromium or Helium adds fails at run time instead of shipping until the Bench finds it.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: services/network/network_service_network_delegate.cc (OnBeforeURLRequest), services/network/url_loader.h (read-only accessor), services/network/BUILD.gn (network_service deps)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #257. The decision is services/network/aerie/request_policy.cc (overlay).
The hook gathers the request URL (the redirect target on a redirect), the
traffic annotation, and facts about the carrying URLLoaderFactory: whether its
process is a real renderer, whether it is trusted, and whether it locks the
request initiator. A request is skipped only when the factory is positively a
renderer's (real renderer process, untrusted, initiator lock). A request with
no URLLoader (WebSocket, certificate fetch, DNS over HTTPS), from a utility
process, or from a trusted or unlocked factory is judged. A page cannot set
any of these facts.

A refusal returns ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ADMINISTRATOR, which nothing else in the
browser returns for a network request, so the Bench can tell it from the
ERR_BLOCKED_BY_CLIENT of the ad blocker and of the dummy-origin refusals.

Limits (see docs/network-endpoints.md, "Limits"): this hook sees URL requests
only. Renderer traffic, raw DNS sockets, QUIC alternative services, CORS
preflight (it takes its request's decision), WebRTC and other non-URL sockets
are outside it. Preconnect and name lookups are judged by patch network/0003.
Design borrowed from Crest (pauljoda/Crest, MPL-2.0); no code is copied.

